From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] choose the profile by the devices it offers, not by the
 PinePhone's names

This replaces callaudiod because PulseAudio 17 and PipeWire 1.2 build one
card profile per UCM device instead of one profile with a port per device
-- but it then hardcodes the profile names the PinePhone's UCM happens to
produce, and every other device with a Voice Call verb produces different
ones. The Pixel 2 XL has 'HiFi', 'Voice Call (Earpiece)' and 'Voice Call
(Speaker)': its voice verb declares no capture device, because a call's
microphone never reaches the CPU on that board, so the profiles carry one
device each and HiFi is not decorated at all.

Three things follow, none of them PinePhone-specific:

  - a suffix list needs the single-device names as well, and a profile that
    is just the verb has to be usable when no suffix matches at all;
  - a verb need not have a source, so the microphone half of a mode change
    must be skippable rather than raise StopIteration;
  - a phone has more than one card the moment a Bluetooth headset connects,
    so the main card is the one that can carry a call, not the only one.

The PinePhone's own selection is unchanged: its decorated names are still
tried first and still match first.
--- a/pinephone-callaudiod	2026-08-27 11:06:16.778224694 +0200
+++ b/pinephone-callaudiod	2026-08-27 11:06:16.779586187 +0200
@@ -70,14 +70,24 @@
 	def __init__(self):
 		main_card_name = None
 		hdmi_card_name = None
+		other_card_name = None
 
+		# A phone has more than one card as soon as a Bluetooth headset
+		# connects, so the main card is the one that can carry a call
+		# rather than the only one there is.
 		for card_name in Pactl.list_cards():
 			if 'hdmi' in card_name:
-				assert hdmi_card_name is None
 				hdmi_card_name = card_name
-			else:
-				assert main_card_name is None
+			elif any(
+				profile_name.startswith('Voice Call')
+				for profile_name in Pactl.list_available_profiles(card_name)
+			):
 				main_card_name = card_name
+			elif other_card_name is None:
+				other_card_name = card_name
+
+		if main_card_name is None:
+			main_card_name = other_card_name
 
 		assert main_card_name is not None
 
@@ -92,16 +102,16 @@
 		return self.__main_card_name
 
 	@property
-	def main_card_hifi_source_name(self) -> str:
+	def main_card_hifi_source_name(self) -> str | None:
 		if self.__main_card_hifi_source_name is None:
-			self.__main_card_hifi_source_name = next(Pactl.list_sources())
+			self.__main_card_hifi_source_name = next(Pactl.list_sources(), None)
 
 		return self.__main_card_hifi_source_name
 
 	@property
-	def main_card_voice_call_source_name(self) -> str:
+	def main_card_voice_call_source_name(self) -> str | None:
 		if self.__main_card_voice_call_source_name is None:
-			self.__main_card_voice_call_source_name = next(Pactl.list_sources())
+			self.__main_card_voice_call_source_name = next(Pactl.list_sources(), None)
 
 		return self.__main_card_voice_call_source_name
 
@@ -164,6 +174,11 @@
 			profile_name = f'{profile_name} ({profile_suffix})'
 			found_profile = True
 			break
+	else:
+		# Where a verb's profiles hold a single device each, the profile is
+		# not decorated at all: the Pixel 2 XL's HiFi profile is plain
+		# 'HiFi', next to 'Voice Call (Earpiece)' and 'Voice Call (Speaker)'.
+		found_profile = profile_name in available_profiles
 
 	assert found_profile
 
@@ -181,6 +196,11 @@
 		case Mode.CALL:
 			source = pulseaudio_state.main_card_voice_call_source_name
 
+	# On the Pixel 2 XL a call's microphone never reaches the CPU -- the DSP
+	# takes it straight off the codec -- so the voice profile has no source.
+	if source is None:
+		return
+
 	match choice.mic:
 		case Mic.MUTED:
 			subprocess.run([
@@ -244,10 +264,13 @@
 			'Headphones, Headset',
 			'Headphones, Mic',
 			'Mic, Speaker', # HiFi mode uses speakers by default, not earpiece.
+			'Headphones',
+			'Speaker',
 		),
 		speaker_forced_profile_suffixes=(
 			'Headset, Speaker',
 			'Mic, Speaker',
+			'Speaker',
 		),
 	)
 	__call_mode_choice = Choice(
@@ -257,10 +280,13 @@
 			'Headphones, Headset',
 			'Headphones, Mic',
 			'Earpiece, Mic',
+			'Headphones',
+			'Earpiece',
 		),
 		speaker_forced_profile_suffixes=(
 			'Headset, Speaker',
 			'Mic, Speaker',
+			'Speaker',
 		),
 	)
 
